@flexiarg operator/reproduce-on-the-current-version-before-reporting-upstream
@title Reproduce On The Current Version Before Reporting A Bug Upstream
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-1relYm turn-8mX1Ks
@parent operator/pin-the-defect-with-its-evidence
@context The agent found a bug in a dependency on an old version and wants to report it to the maintainers.

! conclusion: Install a current version, rerun the reproduction there, search the issue tracker for the bug, and only then draft the report (as a draft, not filed).

  + IF:
    The operator says it is worth reporting only if it reproduces on a current version, and that the one tested is old.

  + HOWEVER:
    The bug may already be fixed upstream and a report would waste the maintainers' time or look careless.

  + THEN:
    Install a current version, rerun the reproduction there, search the issue tracker for the bug, and only then draft the report (as a draft, not filed).

  + BECAUSE:
    A bug fixed since the old version is not a bug in the current one.
